  "notes": "IMAGE CONFLICT at 1,4 (Hasdrubal's unit): the gridded map 014.jpg (old CCA_maps image) shows an HC block (strength 3) there, which would give the Carthaginians 2 HC / 0 HI. The image the scenario page actually embeds today (/ancients/images/014_Great_Plains.png, saved as 014_alt.png) shows an H block (strength 4) at 1,4 with the same positions for everything else, which matches the roster table (1 HI, 1 HC). Page forum posts also say the GMT scenario book has Heavy Infantry with Hasdrubal and that the old map/Vassal module was wrong. Transcribed as HI per the current page image + roster. All other placements are identical in both images (alt image rescaled and gridded to confirm). Open battlefield: no terrain tiles anywhere. No Special Rules section on the page. War Council names the Carthaginian commander 'Hasdrubal Gisgo'; the map caption reads 'Hasdrubal'. Masinissa's caption is partly hidden by the LC block at 7,0 but reads 'Masinissa' (same spelling as the historical text); his portrait is on the LC block at 6,1."
